{
  "choices": [
    {
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"source_routes\": [\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0421\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The impact of sarcopenia on the efficacy and safety of immune checkpoint inhibitors in patients with solid tumours\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究作为非微生物宿主因素的对照案例，显示低肌肉量在实体瘤（尤其肺癌）中未降低 ICI 疗效或增加毒性，挑战了传统预后假设。可用于综述局限性与异质性章节，强调在评估微生物组效应时需区分并校正身体成分等混杂变量，避免将非微生物因素导致的疗效差异误归因于菌群。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0422\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut Associated Metabolites Enhance PD-L1 Blockade Efficacy in Prostate Cancer\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供前列腺癌模型中特定花生四烯酸代谢物（16(R)-HETE, 6-Keto-PGE1）上调外泌体 PD-L1 从而增强抗 PD-L1 疗效的机制证据。可用于微生物特征章节列举特定代谢物标志物，并在机制章节阐述“肠 - 肿瘤代谢轴”如何通过调节检查点分子密度介导疗效，尽管具体产菌尚未鉴定。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0423\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Targeting molecular pathways to control immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicities\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述将微生物组与特定细胞因子（IL-6, IL-17）及整合素通路联系起来，构建了微生物介导免疫毒性（irAEs）的分子框架。可用于机制章节解释微生物如何通过全身炎症反应间接影响治疗窗口，并在局限性章节指出当前多聚焦毒性机制而缺乏直接增效机制的定量数据，提示疗效与毒性平衡的复杂性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiota and metabolites associate with outcomes of immune checkpoint inhibitor–treated unresectable hepatocellular carcinoma\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供肝癌队列中 Lachnoclostridium 富集与次级胆汁酸（UDCA/UCA）水平正相关且预测更好 PFS/ORR 的观察性证据。可用于临床证据章节展示特定癌种的微生物标志物，在特征章节列举有益菌属，并在机制章节提出“微生物 - 胆汁酸轴”作为潜在介导通路，同时注明其限于病毒性肝癌背景。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0425\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Microbial dysbiosis and childhood asthma development: Integrated role of the airway and gut microbiome, environmental exposures, and host metabolic and immune response\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"虽聚焦哮喘，但详细阐述了短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）通过抑制 NF-κB、促进 Tregs 分化调节免疫的通用机制。可用于机制章节作为背景理论，解释微生物代谢物系统性调节适应性免疫的生物学基础，类比其在肿瘤免疫中的潜在作用，但需明确区分疾病模型并标注外推的不确定性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0426\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"1038P Impact of metastatic location on immune-checkpoint inhibitors efficacy in patients with different solid tumours\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供大样本数据显示转移负荷（≥3 个）显著降低 ICI 疗效，而单发转移部位无差异。可用于局限性与异质性章节，强调肿瘤负荷和解剖位置等临床变量是强效预测因子，在评估微生物组独立贡献时必须加以控制，防止将临床分期差异误读为微生物效应。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0427\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Abstract 2377: Gut microbiome modulation by a black raspberry nectar for improving anti-PD1 therapy effectiveness in pre-clinical cancer models\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"展示黑树莓花蜜通过增加 Lachnospiraceae/Blautia 及 L-肉碱水平增强小鼠抗 PD-1 疗效的饮食干预案例。可用于机制章节提出非传统代谢物（L-肉碱）的潜在作用，并在干预章节作为饮食调节可行性的临床前证据，同时指出人类疗效数据缺失及因果链条未完全证实的局限。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0428\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Comparison of baseline gut microbiome features between response subgroups of patients (pts) with advanced melanoma undergoing immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) therapy.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"在黑色素瘤中发现响应者富集 F. prausnitzii 等 SCFA 产生菌，且高丰度与无 irAEs 相关。可用于特征章节列举具体有益菌种，并在机制章节探讨 SCFAs 可能在平衡疗效与毒性中的双重作用，同时强调观察性研究无法确立因果及“无 irAEs 却有效”的反直觉现象需进一步验证。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0429\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Enfortumab vedotin following platinum-based chemotherapy and immune checkpoint inhibitors for advanced urothelial carcinoma: response, survival and safety analysis from a multicentre real-world Japanese cohort.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供尿路上皮癌 ICI 失败后 ADC 治疗的真实世界数据，不涉及微生物机制。可用于局限性与未来方向章节，作为 ICI 耐药后替代疗法的背景基准，说明在微生物干预尚未标准化前，现有二线治疗的实际效能，界定微生物组研究在解决耐药问题上的潜在补充地位而非唯一方案。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0430\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Microbiome bacterial influencers of host immunity and response to immunotherapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"系统综述了跨癌种有益/有害菌属（如 Ruminococcaceae, Akkermansiaceae）、代谢物（SCFAs, 肌苷）及免疫通路（TLR, Treg 平衡）。可用于特征章节汇总分类学标志物，机制章节详述分子路径，干预章节评估 FMT/益生菌现状，并在局限性章节指出观察性关联为主及跨研究异质性大的问题。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0431\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"β-catenin in dendritic cells negatively regulates CD8 T cell immune responses through the immune checkpoint molecule Tim-3 4802\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"阐明 DC 内β-catenin 通过上调 Tim-3 抑制 CD8+ T 细胞的机制，虽未直接涉及肠道菌群，但提供了检查点分子在抗原呈递细胞层面的调控范例。可用于机制章节补充非 PD-1/CTLA-4 的免疫检查点调控路径，提示微生物可能通过影响 DC 功能状态间接调节此类通路，丰富机制网络。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0432\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The gut microbiome affects response of treatments in HER2‐negative advanced gastric cancer\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"在胃癌中发现 Lactobacillus 丰度与 ICI 单药及联合治疗响应正相关，且联合治疗微生物特征非简单叠加。可用于临床证据章节展示治疗特异性标志物，特征章节列举胃癌有益菌，机制章节提及氨基酸/能量代谢通路差异，并强调联合治疗背景下微生物效应的复杂性与情境依赖性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0433\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The relationship between gut microbiota and cancer immune response and immunotherapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"全面综述了 Faecalibacterium/Akkermansia 等有益菌、SCFAs/色氨酸代谢物等机制通路及 FMT/益生菌干预策略。可用于特征章节汇总跨癌种标志物，机制章节详述 AhR/HDAC 等信号通路，干预章节评估临床转化进展，并在局限性章节指出 SCFAs 双重作用及缺乏大规模 RCT 的现状。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0434\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Abstract PS2-07-12: Gut microbiome composition predicts pathologic complete response in patients with early-stage HER2-positive breast cancer receiving neoadjuvant HER2-targeted therapy +/- immunotherapy with pembrolizumab\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供乳腺癌新辅助治疗中微生物组预测 pCR 的初步数据，显示含免疫治疗组特有微生物特征及腹泻与多样性关联。可用于临床证据章节展示早期肿瘤及联合治疗场景下的预测潜力，特征章节列举乳腺癌特异性菌种线索，同时注明样本量小、仅为相关性且菌种功能未知的局限。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0435\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"A comprehensive review of mechanisms underlying resistance to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述了微生物组通过 TLR 信号、髓系细胞稳态及代谢物（丁酸盐）调节 ICI 耐药的机制，并区分了肿瘤内在与外在耐药因素。可用于特征章节列举关键菌属，机制章节详述 DC 激活与 T 细胞调节路径，并在局限性章节强调多数机制源于动物模型及跨癌种异质性，需警惕过度外推。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0436\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Abstract 6699: Delineating germline, tumor and extrinsic factors driving mucosal melanoma (MM) risk and response to immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) treatment\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"描述黏膜黑色素瘤队列中肠道与局部微生物组同步采集及多组学整合的研究设计，尚无疗效关联结果。可用于局限性与未来方向章节，作为罕见肿瘤亚型研究方法的范例，强调区分全身与局部微生物信号的必要性，并指出当前缺乏该亚型实证数据及需进一步探索可改变风险因素。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0437\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gene-level gut microbiome signatures as predictive biomarkers for response to immune checkpoint inhibitors across multiple cancer types\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提出基因水平微生物特征（如 nitrilase 通路）比分类学特征更能预测 CICB 疗效，且受年龄和治疗策略影响。可用于特征章节论证功能基因标志物的优势，机制章节关联氮代谢与 T 细胞调节，并在局限性章节强调跨队列泛化性受治疗背景限制及年龄分层带来的复杂性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0438\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gastrointestinal cancer resistance to treatment: the role of microbiota\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"聚焦消化道肿瘤，详述 Fusobacterium 抑制 NK 细胞、Barnesiella 增强 T 细胞浸润等机制及 SCFAs/胆汁酸调节作用。可用于特征章节列举 GI 癌特异性菌群，机制章节详述免疫细胞训练与代谢调控路径，干预章节提及益生菌/FMT 潜力，同时注明主要基于临床前模型及 GI 癌特异性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Harnessing the gut microbiome for improved immune checkpoint inhibition in colorectal cancer immunotherapy: a narrative Review.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"针对 MSS/pMMR 结直肠癌，综述了 Akkermansia/Fusobacterium 等菌种、SCFAs/4-HPA 等代谢物机制及 FMT/饮食干预现状。可用于特征章节列举难治亚型标志物，机制章节详述 TLR4/NF-κB 通路，干预章节评估非抗生素策略，并在局限性章节指出 A. muciniphila 作用矛盾及缺乏标准化方案的问题。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0440\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"An observational study to evaluate pattern of usage of immune checkpoint inhibitors in the 1st line treatment of various advanced solid tumors, their efficacy and their toxicity profile.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供真实世界 ICI 一线治疗的疗效基线（PR 率 31.25%）及毒性谱（肺炎/皮疹高发），无微生物数据。可用于局限性与异质性章节，作为评估微生物组效应时的临床背景参照，说明在未控制微生物状态下的平均疗效水平，并提示真实世界毒性管理策略可能间接反映免疫激活强度。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0441\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) as \\\"chemotherapy (Ctx) sensitization\\\" strategy in advanced solid tumours\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"显示在难治性实体瘤中 ICI 序贯化疗未显著改善 PFS，提供阴性结果案例。可用于局限性与异质性章节，说明 ICI 并非普遍增敏化疗，提示微生物介导的增效作用可能具有高度特异性或条件依赖性，强调在寻找生物标志物时需考虑治疗序列和肿瘤类型的特定背景。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0442\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The microbiome and gynaecological cancer development, prevention and therapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提及 A. muciniphila 恢复 PD-1 疗效的小鼠 FMT 证据及双歧杆菌/拟杆菌的免疫调节作用。可用于机制章节补充妇科肿瘤背景下的微生物 - 免疫互作线索，干预章节作为 FMT 克服耐药的早期概念验证，但需明确主要基于动物模型及妇科癌背景，外推至实体瘤通用机制需谨慎。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Non-small cell lung cancer patients treated with Anti-PD1 immunotherapy show distinct microbial signatures and metabolic pathways according to progression-free survival and PD-L1 status\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"在 NSCLC 中鉴定 Alistipes 促进疗效、Streptococcus 抑制疗效的物种水平标志物，并量化预测效能（AUC 0.74）。可用于临床证据章节展示稳健标志物，特征章节列举具体菌种，机制章节探讨菌群网络结构与代谢通路作用，并在局限性章节指出种族差异及化疗预处理对菌群的扰动影响。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0444\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Microbial metabolic pathways guide response to immune checkpoint blockade therapy.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提出 MEP 通路（HMBPP 激活 Vδ2 T 细胞）促免疫与核黄素通路（5-OP-RU 激活 MAIT 细胞）抑免疫的双向机制，强调功能通路优于物种组成。可用于特征章节论证功能标志物价值，机制章节详述人类特有 T 细胞亚群调控路径，并在局限性章节指出体外验证为主及肿瘤特异性差异。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0445\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The future of affordable cancer immunotherapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"讨论微生物组疗法（FMT/SCFA 监测）作为低成本增强 ICI 疗效策略的潜力。可用于干预章节评估经济可及性与转化前景，并在局限性章节指出当前仅有轻微成功及标准化困难，强调在资源有限环境中开发廉价微生物干预措施的必要性及现有证据的观察性局限。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0446\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Multi-omics analysis of saccharomyces boulardii supplementation reveals coordinated microbiome, metabolic, and immune signaling changes accompanying tumor suppression\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"展示 S. boulardii 通过产生 5-HIAA 及促进 IPA 生成激活 AhR 通路抑制结直肠癌生长的机制。可用于机制章节详述色氨酸代谢物 -AhR 轴介导的免疫调节，干预章节作为益生菌替代 FMT 的安全可行案例，同时注明皮下移植瘤模型及间接因果推断的局限。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0447\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Microbial metabolites and their influence on the tumor microenvironment\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述 SCFAs/胆汁酸/色氨酸代谢物通过 HDAC/GPCR/AhR 等通路重塑 T 细胞/巨噬细胞代谢状态的机制。可用于特征章节列举代谢物类别，机制章节详述免疫细胞代谢重编程路径，并在局限性章节指出多数证据源于回顾性队列或动物模型，因果链条需更多 RCT 支持及代谢物多效性风险。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0448\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Role of gut microbiome in the outcome of lymphoma patients treated with checkpoint inhibitors—The MicroLinf Study\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"在淋巴瘤中发现 Lachnospira 富集与响应相关，Enterobacteriaceae 与非响应相关。可用于局限性与异质性章节作为血液肿瘤对比案例，强调肿瘤类型特异性导致微生物标志物可能不同，提示实体瘤结论不可直接泛化至所有癌症类型，需严格界定研究范围。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0449\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut Microbiota Metabolites and Chronic Diseases: Interactions, Mechanisms, and Therapeutic Strategies\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"详述 SCFAs/胆汁酸在慢性病中调节 Th17/Treg 平衡及巨噬细胞极化的通用机制。可用于机制章节提供微生物 - 免疫互作的生物学基础背景，解释代谢物系统性调节免疫稳态的原理，类比其在肿瘤免疫中的潜在作用，但需明确区分非肿瘤疾病背景及缺乏 ICI 直接数据。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0450\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut Microbiota and Response to Immunotherapeutic Drugs in Oncology: More Questions Than Answers\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"汇总了 Bifidobacterium/Akkermansia 等与疗效相关的菌种列表及抗生素负面影响，强调机制未知及转化障碍。可用于特征章节列举早期观察到的标志物，并在局限性章节深入讨论结果异质性、缺乏共识及监管/安全挑战，界定领域当前“问题多于答案”的发展阶段。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0451\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Harnessing the Gut Microbiome in Cancer Immunotherapy: Mechanisms, Challenges, and Routes to Personalized Medicine—A Systematic Review\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"系统综述了 SCFAs/PSA/I3A 等代谢物机制、特定菌株作用及 FMT/益生菌干预挑战。可用于特征章节汇总标志物，机制章节详述 GPCR/TLR/AhR 通路，干预章节评估个性化医疗路线，并在局限性章节指出临床数据有限、供体差异及缺乏实时监测工具等转化瓶颈。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0452\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Sucralose and the Gut–Immune Axis: Emerging Evidence Linking Dysbiosis, Barrier Alterations, and Implications for Colitis and Colorectal Cancer Immunotherapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提出三氯蔗糖通过减少产丁酸菌及降低精氨酸/瓜氨酸水平削弱 CD8+ T 细胞功能从而降低 ICI 疗效的机制。可用于机制章节详述饮食成分负面调节路径，干预章节警示人工甜味剂风险，并在局限性章节强调人类数据限于非 CRC 队列及动物模型剂量依赖性，需进一步验证临床因果。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0453\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Effect of dual immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) by the time of infusion in advanced non–small cell lung cancer (NSCLC): A secondary analysis of CCTG BR34 trial.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"显示双免疫联合治疗中下午输注优于上午，与单药研究结果相反。可用于局限性与异质性章节，强调时间治疗效应受治疗方案（联合 vs 单药）及肿瘤类型影响，提示宿主节律与微生物组可能存在复杂交互，机制尚未阐明且不能简单外推至所有 ICI 场景。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0454\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Eating away cancer: the potential of diet and the microbiome for shaping immunotherapy outcome\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述高纤维/植物性饮食通过 SCFAs/胆汁酸增强 ICB 疗效的机制，警示商业益生菌及西式饮食风险。可用于机制章节详述饮食 - 微生物 - 免疫轴，干预章节评估饮食调节策略，并在局限性章节指出多为观察性或临床前数据、黑色素瘤为主及益生菌效果情境依赖性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0455\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiome in gastrointestinal neoplasms: from mechanisms to precision therapeutic strategies\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"聚焦 GI 肿瘤，详述 F. nucleatum 耐药机制、FMT 恢复敏感性（CXCR3+ CD8+ T 细胞）及工程菌策略。可用于特征章节列举 GI 癌特异性标志物，机制章节详述 AhR/IDO1 通路，干预章节评估精准治疗策略，并在局限性章节指出缺乏大规模 RCT 及供体筛选争议。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0456\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The Resistance Mechanisms of Checkpoint Inhibitors in Solid Tumors\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"将微生物群列为 ICI 耐药六大机制之一，详述交叉反应/DC 激活机制及双歧杆菌/纤维的正面作用。可用于特征章节汇总早期关键菌种，机制章节补充抗原呈递缺陷之外的微生物调节路径，并在局限性章节强调多为小鼠模型及人类因果未确立，需结合其他耐药机制综合考量。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0457\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The tumor microbiome and cancer immunotherapy: A systematic review of a new frontier beyond the gut.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"聚焦肿瘤内微生物群而非肠道，提出局部免疫激活/抑制/耗竭机制。可用于机制章节补充局部微环境平行机制，区分全身（肠道）与局部（肿瘤）微生物效应，并在局限性章节指出缺乏量化证据及肿瘤类型特异性，强调空间异质性对机制解析的挑战。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0458\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Examining the impact of the microbiome on cancer immunotherapy outcomes: A review\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"概括 Akkermansia/Bifidobacterium 等有益菌及代谢物/细胞因子/抗原呈递三大机制类别。可用于特征章节提供高层级分类框架，机制章节结构化讨论路径，干预章节列举策略，并在局限性章节指出多为相关性描述及转化挑战，适合作为概念性背景素材。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0459\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The circadian-microbiome-immune axis in colorectal cancer: mechanisms of spatiotemporal immunosuppression and chronotherapeutic horizons\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提出昼夜节律 - 微生物 - 免疫轴，详述睡眠剥夺致 Lactobacillus 减少/TCA 增加进而抑制 CD8+ T 细胞的时空机制。可用于机制章节引入时间生物学维度，解释 MDSCs 时相性积累路径，并在局限性章节强调基于小鼠模型及人类最佳给药窗口未确立，需验证 TIS 框架。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0460\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Therapeutic targeting of the host-microbiota-immune axis: implications for precision health\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述厚壁菌门（F. prausnitzii 等）通过丁酸盐/Treg/屏障功能调节 ICI 疗效的机制及 FMT 因果证据。可用于特征章节列举关键菌属，机制章节详述代谢与屏障路径，干预章节评估 FMT 潜力，同时注明多为动物模型推论及厚壁菌门内部功能异质性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0461\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Immune checkpoint inhibitors in melanoma: mechanisms, immune cell interactions, and the tumour microenvironment\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"聚焦皮肤微生物群而非肠道，讨论皮肤菌群多样性与 ICI 响应关联。可用于局限性与异质性章节作为解剖部位特异性案例，区分皮肤与肠道微生物生态位及机制差异，提示局部微生物环境也是重要调节因素，避免将肠道结论泛化至所有微生物 - 免疫互作。\"\n},\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n  \"CH02\",\n  \"CH03\",\n  \"CH04\"\n],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"从 SCFAs、分子模拟及菌株特异性三维度解析肺癌 ICI 疗效与 irAEs 机制，提出“智能 FMT\"概念。可用于特征章节细化至代谢通路与菌株水平，机制章节详述抗原交叉反应路径，干预章节展望精准 FMT 策略，同时注明分子模拟多为生物信息学预测及需功能验证。\"\n    },\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0463\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The Great Debate at'Immunotherapy Bridge', Naples, December 5, 2019\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"呈现专家关于菌种特异性证据不足及饮食直接免疫效应的辩论观点。可用于局限性与异质性章节引入“功能优于组成”及饮食独立作用的争议视角，提示单纯依赖菌种分类的局限，强调需考虑饮食等混杂因素及不同治疗策略下的机制差异。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0464\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Potential mechanisms and targeting strategies of the gut microbiota in antitumor immunity and immunotherapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"详述 MAMPs/代谢物/分子模拟/屏障四大机制及特定菌株（A. muciniphila, B. fragilis）作用，汇总临床试验。可用于特征章节列举关键菌种，机制章节提供全面分子通路，干预章节评估工程菌/FMT 进展，并在局限性章节强调多为临床前数据及菌株特异性差异。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0465\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Development of a novel immune-related toxicity grading system for predicting outcomes in patients with solid tumours treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI).\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"建立 irAEs 多器官受累评分与生存正相关的临床证据，未涉及微生物。可用于局限性与异质性章节，作为“毒性 - 疗效”表型关联的基准，提示系统性免疫激活的重要性，为后续探索微生物介导该现象的机制提供临床现象学依据，但需区分相关与因果。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0466\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Shaping the Future of Immunotherapy Targets and Biomarkers in Melanoma and Non-Melanoma Cutaneous Cancers\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"汇总黑色素瘤中双歧杆菌/Ruminococcaceae 与疗效关联及 FMT 恢复响应的临床数据，提出代谢物/抗原交叉反应机制。可用于临床证据章节展示 FMT 概念验证，特征章节列举皮肤癌标志物，机制章节补充局部与全身互作线索，并在局限性章节强调多为观察性及小样本试验。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0467\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Managing Resistance to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors in Lung Cancer: Treatment and Novel Strategies.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述肺癌 ICI 耐药机制及联合策略，未直接涉及肠道菌群。可用于局限性与未来方向章节，作为通用耐药背景框架，提示微生物组可能通过调节 TME 或 T 细胞启动间接影响耐药，但需明确本文未证实菌群作用，仅作为机制探索的潜在方向之一。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0468\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"From Womb to World: Unravelling the Microbiota′s Impact on Health and Disease\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述微生物多样性/Bacteroides 与 ICI 响应关联及 FMT 增强 T 细胞反应证据，讨论方法学挑战。可用于特征章节汇总早期标志物，机制章节提及 T 细胞激活路径，干预章节介绍 FMT 制剂现状，并在局限性章节强调测序异质性导致结果不可比及因果推断困难。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0469\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiota-mediated immunomodulation in tumor\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"全面综述 Ruminococcaceae/Akkermansia 等标志物、PAMPs/代谢物机制及抗生素/FMT 影响。可用于临床证据章节汇总多癌种数据，特征章节列举关键菌属，机制章节详述 TLR/NF-κB/GPRs 通路，干预章节评估策略，并在局限性章节指出回顾性研究为主及机制双向性。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"The impact of gut microbiota modulation on responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"荟萃分析确认 Akkermansia/Bifidobacterium 富集与疗效正相关、抗生素与疗效负相关及 FMT 提高 ORR。可用于临床证据章节提供群体水平统计关联，特征章节汇总高置信度菌属，干预章节量化 FMT 效应，同时注明未分层癌种及缺乏具体机制数据。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0471\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut Microbiota and Cancer: From Pathogenesis to Therapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"汇总 2018-2019 关键研究，指出 Akkermansia/Bifidobacterium 与 PD-1 响应相关，B. fragilis 与 CTLA-4 相关，详述 TNF/T 细胞浸润机制。可用于特征章节列举早期里程碑菌种，机制章节补充细胞因子路径，干预章节提及益生菌缓解副作用，同时注明时效性及动物模型局限。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0472\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Immunometabolism: The role of gut‐derived microbial metabolites in optimising immune response during checkpoint inhibitor therapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"详述 SCFAs 促进 CD8+ T 细胞功能、色氨酸代谢抑制 T 细胞及益生菌矛盾证据。可用于特征章节列举代谢物标志物，机制章节详述 HDAC/GPCR/IDO1 通路，干预章节警示商业益生菌风险，并在局限性章节指出小样本研究为主及 IDO 抑制剂临床失败教训。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0473\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Abstract 6687: Evaluation of a new co-cultured microbiome ecosystem therapy candidate (MaaT034) for clinical testing as adjuvant/neoadjuvant to immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumors\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"展示共培养微生物组 MaaT034 通过分泌 SCFAs/次级胆汁酸及促进 moDC 成熟增强 ICI 敏感性的体外机制。可用于机制章节提供标准化菌群产品作用范例，干预章节介绍新型共培养疗法，同时注明仅限体外模型及“首次”声明需视为营销主张，缺乏体内验证。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Tumor microenvironment-mediated resistance to immune checkpoint inhibitors in non-small cell lung cancer: Mechanisms, combination strategies and clinical perspectives (Review)\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"在 NSCLC 背景下提及 Akkermansia/Bifidobacterium 有益及 Fusobacterium 作用不确定，强调系统性因素与 TME 交互。可用于特征章节列举肺癌特异性线索，机制章节讨论系统性炎症调节，并在局限性章节指出微生物干预仍属探索阶段及需疾病特异性验证，避免过度泛化。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0475\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Exploring Gut–Brain Interaction Disorders: Mechanisms and Translational Therapies Crossing Neurology to Gastroenterology\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述聚焦肠 - 脑轴及功能性胃肠病，未涉及实体瘤或 ICI 疗效，仅泛泛提及微生物组免疫调节。因缺乏肿瘤特异性数据及 ICI 相关机制，无法直接支持本综述核心论点，故不纳入。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0476\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut metabolites: key factors in the cross-talk between the gut microbiota and tumor immunotherapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"详述 TMAO/SCFAs 等代谢物在不同肿瘤中的双向作用及 AhR/FXR/TLR4 等受体机制。可用于特征章节强调代谢物情境依赖性，机制章节详述免疫细胞分化路径，干预章节评估靶向代谢物策略，并在局限性章节指出动物模型为主及临床数据回顾性局限。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0477\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Targeting the gut microbiota-metabolite-immune axis in cancer immunotherapy: mechanistic interplay, therapeutic strategies, and translational applications-a narrative review\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH04\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"跨癌种汇总微生物标志物及 SCFAs/色氨酸/胆汁酸/肌苷四大核心代谢物机制，评估 FMT/工程菌转化现状。可用于特征章节列举多癌种标志物，机制章节详述双向调节路径，干预章节评估策略挑战，并在局限性章节指出叙事性综述偏倚及缺乏大规模 RCT。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0478\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Cross-cohort gut microbiome associations with immune checkpoint inhibitor response in advanced melanoma\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH01\",\n    \"CH02\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供跨队列分析显示通用标志物难以复现，但 Bifidobacterium/Roseburia/Akkermansia 具部分一致性。可用于临床证据章节警示异质性，特征章节列举稳健候选菌种，并在局限性章节深入讨论队列效应、批次偏差及机器学习模型泛化失败的方法学挑战。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0479\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"Gut Metabolites and Breast Cancer: The Continuum of Dysbiosis, Breast Cancer Risk, and Potential Breast Cancer Therapy\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH03\",\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述 SCFAs/肌苷等在实体瘤中调节 ICI 疗效的机制及乳腺癌特异性代谢物作用。可用于机制章节提供代谢物 - 免疫互作背景，支持假设生成，并在局限性章节强调乳腺癌直接临床数据稀缺及多为外推自其他癌种，需警惕癌种特异性差异。\"\n},\n    {\n  \"source_handle\": \"P0480\",\n  \"paper_title\": \"A prospective translational study investigating the association of gut microbiome (GM) diversity with pathological complete response (pCR) after neoadjuvant treatment in early stage rectal and esophageal cancers.\",\n  \"chapter_ids\": [\n    \"CH05\"\n  ],\n  \"specific_usable_material\": \"描述胃肠道肿瘤新辅助治疗中 GM 多样性与 pCR 关联的研究方案，尚无结果且不涉及 ICI。可用于局限性与未来方向章节，作为非 ICI 治疗背景下微生物组研究的对照案例，提示 GM 在不同治疗模式中作用可能不同，并强调前瞻性设计的重要性及当前知识缺口。\"\n}\n  ]\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to route a batch of 60 sources (P0421 to P0480) to a pre-defined 5-chapter outline for a review on \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\".\n\nI need to:\n1. Read each source's B_review_planning card carefully.\n2. Determine which chapter(s) each source best fits into based on its actual content (not just title or claims).\n3. Write a specific_usable_material description (80-150 Chinese characters) for each source that is routed.\n4. For sources that are not relevant, leave chapter_ids empty and explain briefly.\n5. Ensure I don't over-claim causality or mechanisms where the source only provides correlation.\n6. Maintain the source_handle exactly as provided.\n7. Return JSON only.\n\nLet me analyze each source:\n\n**P0421**: Sarcopenia and ICI efficacy - This is about muscle mass, NOT gut microbiome. It's a host factor but not microbiome-related. Should be routed to CH05 (limitations/heterogeneity) as a non-microbiome host factor example, or excluded. Given the review focuses on gut microbiome, this is tangential. I'll route to CH05 as a contrast example of non-microbiome host factors.\n\n**P0422**: Gut metabolites (16(R)-HETE, 6-Keto-PGE1) enhancing PD-L1 blockade in prostate cancer. This is mechanistic (metabolites). Fits CH03 (mechanisms).\n\n**P0423**: Review on targeting molecular pathways for ICI toxicities. Mentions microbiome as a factor but focuses on irAEs. Could fit CH03 (mechanisms of toxicity) or CH05. Given it's abstract-only and focuses on toxicity mechanisms, CH03 or CH05.\n\n**P0424**: Gut microbiota and metabolites in HCC patients on ICI. Clinical evidence with specific bacteria (Lachnoclostridium, Prevotella 9) and metabolites (bile acids). Fits CH01 (clinical evidence) and CH02 (microbial features).\n\n**P0425**: Review on microbiome and childhood asthma. NOT cancer/ICI. This is off-topic for the specific review question. Should be excluded or routed to CH05 as an example of non-cancer microbiome-immune mechanisms that inform general principles. Given the strict focus on solid tumors and ICI, this should probably be excluded (chapter_ids empty).\n\n**P0426**: Metastatic location impact on ICI efficacy. No microbiome data. This is a clinical prognostic factor study. Could be CH05 (heterogeneity/limitations) as a non-microbiome factor. But it's abstract-only and doesn't address microbiome. I'll exclude it (empty chapter_ids).\n\n**P0427**: Black raspberry nectar modulating microbiome to improve anti-PD1 in preclinical models. This is an intervention study (diet → microbiome → ICI). Fits CH04 (interventions) and CH03 (mechanisms - L-carnitine).\n\n**P0428**: Baseline gut microbiome in melanoma ICI patients, SCFA producers. Clinical observational. Fits CH01 (clinical evidence) and CH02 (microbial features).\n\n**P0429**: Enfortumab vedotin after ICI in urothelial carcinoma. No microbiome. This is about ADC therapy after ICI failure. Not relevant to the microbiome-ICI question. Exclude.\n\n**P0430**: Review on microbiome bacterial influencers of immunity and immunotherapy. Comprehensive review. Fits CH02 (microbial features), CH03 (mechanisms), CH04 (interventions).\n\n**P0431**: β-catenin in DCs regulating Tim-3. No microbiome. This is about DC intrinsic signaling. Not directly about gut microbiome. Could be CH03 as a parallel immune mechanism, but it's not microbiome-mediated. Exclude or CH05 as non-microbiome mechanism. I'll exclude as it doesn't address microbiome.\n\n**P0432**: Gut microbiome in HER2-negative gastric cancer on ICI. Clinical evidence with Lactobacillus. Fits CH01, CH02.\n\n**P0433**: Review on gut microbiota and cancer immune response/immunotherapy. Comprehensive. Fits CH02, CH03, CH04.\n\n**P0434**: Gut microbiome predicting pCR in HER2+ breast cancer neoadjuvant therapy +/- pembrolizumab. Clinical evidence. Fits CH01, CH02.\n\n**P0435**: Review on mechanisms of ICI resistance. Includes microbiome section. Fits CH03, CH05.\n\n**P0436**: Abstract on mucosal melanoma microbiome study design. No results yet. This is a study protocol/baseline description. Could be CH05 (methodological considerations) or excluded. I'll route to CH05 as it discusses methodology for integrating gut and tumor microbiome.\n\n**P0437**: Gene-level gut microbiome signatures predicting ICI response across cancers. Clinical evidence with functional genes. Fits CH01, CH02, CH03 (mechanisms via gene pathways).\n\n**P0438**: Review on GI cancer resistance and microbiota. Fits CH02, CH03.\n\n**P0439**: Narrative review on microbiome for CRC immunotherapy. Fits CH02, CH03, CH04.\n\n**P0440**: Observational study on ICI usage patterns and toxicity. No microbiome. Exclude.\n\n**P0441**: ICI as chemotherapy sensitization. No microbiome. Exclude.\n\n**P0442**: Review on microbiome and gynaecological cancer. Mentions FMT and A. muciniphila for PD-1. Fits CH03, CH04.\n\n**P0443**: NSCLC patients on anti-PD1 with microbial signatures. Clinical evidence. Fits CH01, CH02, CH03.\n\n**P0444**: Microbial metabolic pathways guiding ICB response. Mechanistic (MEP pathway, riboflavin). Fits CH03, CH02.\n\n**P0445**: Review on affordable cancer immunotherapy. Mentions microbiome as low-cost option. Fits CH04, CH05.\n\n**P0446**: S. boulardii supplementation multi-omics. Preclinical mechanistic. Fits CH03, CH04.\n\n**P0447**: Review on microbial metabolites and TME. Fits CH03.\n\n**P0448**: Lymphoma patients (NOT solid tumor). This is hematologic malignancy. The review question specifies solid tumors. Should be excluded or CH05 as a contrast. I'll exclude as it's not solid tumor.\n\n**P0449**: Review on gut metabolites and chronic diseases (not cancer). Off-topic. Exclude.\n\n**P0450**: Review \"More Questions Than Answers\" on microbiome and immunotherapy. Fits CH05 (limitations/gaps).\n\n**P0451**: Systematic review on harnessing gut microbiome in cancer immunotherapy. Fits CH02, CH03, CH04, CH05.\n\n**P0452**: Review on sucralose and gut-immune axis, implications for CRC immunotherapy. Dietary intervention angle. Fits CH03, CH04.\n\n**P0453**: Abstract on ICI infusion timing in NSCLC. No microbiome. Exclude.\n\n**P0454**: Review on diet and microbiome for immunotherapy outcome. Fits CH03, CH04.\n\n**P0455**: Review on gut microbiome in GI neoplasms. Fits CH02, CH03, CH04.\n\n**P0456**: Review on ICI resistance mechanisms. Includes microbiome section. Fits CH03, CH05.\n\n**P0457**: Abstract on tumor microbiome (NOT gut). This is about intratumoral microbiome. The review question is about gut microbiome. Could be CH05 as a contrast/complementary perspective. I'll route to CH05.\n\n**P0458**: Abstract on examining microbiome impact on immunotherapy. Review. Fits CH02, CH03.\n\n**P0459**: Review on circadian-microbiome-immune axis in CRC. Mechanistic (TCA, MDSCs). Fits CH03, CH05.\n\n**P0460**: Review on therapeutic targeting of host-microbiota-immune axis. Fits CH03, CH04.\n\n**P0461**: Review on ICI in melanoma, mentions skin microbiome. NOT gut microbiome. Could be CH05 as a contrast. I'll route to CH05.\n\n**P0462**: Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry in lung cancer survivors. Clinical evidence with mechanisms. Fits CH01, CH02, CH03.\n\n**P0463**: Debate report on immunotherapy. Mentions microbiome",
